{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 13, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark to thee my noble traveler bound for Nippon’s fair land\nLet this be thy quest charted with verse so grand\n\nUpon the morn of thy first day do thou arise with haste\nTo Tokyo’s bustling heart where neon lights do waste\nAt Shinjuku’s crossroads gaze with eyes wide bright\nWhere love hotels and gods share the fading night\n\nUpon thy second morn unto Asakusa thou shalt fare\nWhere temples old do whisper to the sky so fair\nAt Sensō-ji’s gate do knead thy palms with prayer\nThen through the market’s labyrinth thy fortune declare\n\nOn the third day let Asakusa’s shadows part\nTo Akiba’s electric dream where robots do play their part\nThrough Akihabara’s lanes with cyber delights beguiled\nDo thou buy some trinket for thy memories beguiled\n\nLo the fourth day calls thee to nature’s embrace\nTo Nikko’s woods where shrines in mist do hide their face\nKegon Falls do leap with thunder and with grace\nWhile torii gates stand tall in the sacred place\n\nBy the fifth day let thy feet turn toward the sea\nTo Yokohama’s port where ships of old do flee\nCup of foreign brew at Motomachi thou shalt quaff\nThen stare at the bay where moon and waves do waff\n\nOn the sixth dawn rise and bid Tokyo farewell\nTo Kyoto’s hanamachi let thy journey swell\nAt Gion’s lantern-lit streets with geisha dreams entwined\nDo thou seek the tea house whose silence shines so kind\n\nThe seventh morn shall gift thee with Fushimi’s might\nWhere breweries hidden spill sake so bright\nThen through Arashiyama’s bamboos walk with care\nWhere the river tells tales of samurai’s lair\n\nOn the eighth day let the Kinkaku-ji’s gold enchanted\nCast its spell upon thy soul so unattainted\nThen through Ryoan-ji’s stones where zen winds do weave\nFind peace amidst the chaos thou dost grieve\n\nLo the ninth day calls thee forth to Nara’s ancient air\nWhere deer with eyes so gentle do stare with prayer\nFeed them thy crackers then to Todai-ji go\nWhere Buddha’s bronze smiles o’er the grass below\n\nBy the tenth dawn let thy spirit be light and keen\nTo Osaka’s heart where takoyaki do sizzle and gleam\nAt Dotonbori’s lights with street food’s feast beguiled\nDo thou laugh and eat as the night’s own jewel\n\nUpon the eleventh morn let thy path inclined be\nTo Hiroshima’s peace where the park doth cry\nThen to Miyajima’s torii where tides do rise and sigh\nLet thy heart feel the weight of time’s sad pie\n\nThe twelfth day shall see thee return to Tokyo’s glow\nWhere Shibuya’s scramble like a dance does flow\nWith one last sushi feast at Tsukiji’s embrace\nBefore thy flight home to thy own foreign place\n\nThus ends thy quest through Japan’s tapestry so wide\nWith memories wrought in verse and rhyme’s sweet tide\nMay thy journey’s echoes linger long and true\nAnd thy heart remain forever in Nippon’s view.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.16029712557792664}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.003225721186026931}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -2.9867587089538574}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0396350733935833}, {"token": "e", "logprob": -0.0018114125123247504}, {"token": " my", "logprob": -2.6546316146850586}, {"token": " noble", "logprob": -0.7794173359870911}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -0.4362308382987976}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.0014013956533744931}, {"token": " bound", "logprob": -0.7521157264709473}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.01648261770606041}, {"token": " Nippon", "logprob": -1.2084847688674927}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.3887452185153961}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -0.4279562830924988}, {"token": " land", "logprob": -1.5746233463287354}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.38444945216178894}, {"token": "Let", "logprob": -1.5926467180252075}, {"token": " this", "logprob": -1.9356576204299927}, {"token": " be", "logprob": -2.5960848331451416}, {"token": " thy", "logprob": -0.21446071565151215}, {"token": " quest", "l